<title>THAILAND: Thai money markets closed for holiday.</title>
<headline>Thai money markets closed for holiday.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Thai money markets were closed on Monday for the Coronation Day public holiday.</p>
<p>The baht eased to 26.110-26.113 per dollar late on Friday from 26.105-26.110 on Friday morning.</p>
<p>The overnight interbank rate rose to 9.75-10.25 percents late on Friday from 9.50-10.00 on Friday morning, traders said.</p>
<p>-- Bangkok newsroom (662) 652-0652</p>
</text>
